ReelEdit: licences
==================

ReelEdit is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify it under
the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by the Free
Software Foundation, either version 2 of the License, or (at your option)
any later version. It comes with NO WARRANTY. See GPLv2 in this directory.

Copyright (C) 2026 Andrew Youll.

!RunImage is one program built from ReelEdit and the parts below, all
linked into it. Each part keeps its own licence. Because some of them are
under the GPL version 2 only (ReelHWAccel), !RunImage as a whole
is distributed under the GNU GPL version 2.

  Part                        Licence                       Its notice here
  ----                        -------                       ---------------
  ReelEdit (its own code)     GPL v2 or later               GPLv2
  MLT 7.42.0 (with ReelEdit's
    patches, built in)        LGPL v2.1 or later            MLT, LGPLv21
  FFmpeg 5.1.10 (riscos-ffmpeg,
    built with --enable-gpl)  GPL v2 or later as built      FFmpeg, GPLv2
  x264                        GPL v2 or later               x264
  ReelHWAccel (the VideoCore
    decoders, vcdec, hevcdec) GPL v2                        ReelHWAccel
  LAME (libmp3lame)           LGPL v2 or later              LAME
  libvorbis, libogg           BSD                           Vorbis, Ogg
  Opus                        BSD                           Opus
  dav1d                       BSD                           dav1d
  libxml2 2.14.5              MIT                           libxml2
  zlib 1.3.1                  zlib                          Toolchain (7)
  UnixLib, PThreadTicker      BSD (parts LGPL v2)           Toolchain (8),
                                                            PThreadTicker
  GCC runtime                 GPL v3 with the GCC Runtime
                              Library Exception             Toolchain (9)

Toolchain is riscos-mesa's licence file, which ReelEdit's build shares:
only its sections 7 (zlib), 8 (UnixLib) and 9 (GCC runtime) apply to
ReelEdit; the rest (Mesa, SDL, GLU, freeglut, OpenAL) isn't in it.

The fonts shown in titles are your computer's own RISC OS fonts; none are
included.

Source code
-----------
The complete source for ReelEdit, its MLT patches and how it's built:
  https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-reeledit
The FFmpeg, x264, ReelHWAccel and other libraries' sources, as built:
  https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-ffmpeg (each release: its devkit and
  the sources it was built from)
  https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-reelhwaccel
MLT 7.42.0: https://github.com/mltframework/mlt (ReelEdit's changes are
in patches/mlt in ReelEdit's source).
libxml2: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2
The toolchain (GCCSDK, UnixLib): https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-crossdev
